// application is responsible for cleanup and recovery in this case.\n    48\ttype Storage interface {\n    49\t\t// TODO(tbg): split this into two interfaces, LogStorage and StateStorage.\n    50\t\n    51\t\t// InitialState returns the saved HardState and ConfState information.\n    52\t\t// The returned HardState may be nil to indicate that no HardState has been\n    53\t\t// persisted yet; IsEmptyHardState treats nil as empty.\n    54\t\t// The returned ConfState must not be nil; if no ConfState has been\n    55\t\t// persisted yet, return an empty ConfState instead.\n    56\t\tInitialState() (*pb.HardState, *pb.ConfState, error)\n    57\t\n    58\t\t// Entries returns a slice of consecutive log entries in the range [lo, hi),\n    59\t\t// starting from lo. The maxSize limits the total size of the log entries\n    60\t\t// returned, but Entries returns at least one entry if any.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
